# Dependencies managed by Renovate (see docs/renovate.md). These rules come last on
# purpose: the last matching pattern wins, and a Renovate PR rewrites the same
# dependency in dozens of directories at once (resyncing a single lockfile pin touches
# every requirements/ directory that constrains it). Leaving them to the per-service rules
# above makes one security bump wait on six or seven reviewers, which is how the PRs go
# stale. Owners of the surrounding code are still requested for the other files of the
# same PR, and anyone can still review these.
**/requirements/**                                     @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/api/tests/requirements.txt                            @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
**/Dockerfile*                                         @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
**/docker-compose*.yml                                 @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/.python-version                                       @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/package.json                                          @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/package-lock.json                                     @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/.renovaterc.jsonc                                     @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/.github/workflows/**                                  @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo
/.github/renovate/**                                   @sanderegg @pcrespov @GitHK @giancarloromeo

